A.XG=s(["In Settings, select the language you will use in the app.","Choose your currency or create a custom one. Currency only changes the code and symbol; it does not convert existing amounts.","Enter your real business name and details so quotes and documents show the correct information.","Then open Profit or Finance and Machines; those sections contain the values that build the price."],t.s)
A.aSw=new B.am("application","FIRST STEPS","Language, currency, and business","Prepare the app before calculating your first job.",A.XG,"If you change currency, manually convert and update every price and cost.",null)
A.aE6=s(["Check your bill or utility and find the current price per kWh for your service type and country.","If the bill has several energy charges, calculate an effective rate: divide the charges you want to recover by the billed kWh.","Use an average or slightly higher rate to cover expensive seasons and consumption changes. Subsidized household rates usually understate workshop or business costs.","Also enter the wattage of every printer and device; use its label, manual, or preferably a power meter."],t.s)
A.aSm=new B.am("application","ENERGY","Set the real kWh cost","Do not use a cheap household rate as a business cost.",A.aE6,"Rates change by country, area, season, and consumption tier. Review important bills and never copy another person's example.",null)
A.aI0=s(["Enter the real cost per kg or liter for each material. When relevant, distribute shipping and purchase taxes so the cost is not understated.","The failure margin reserves material for failed prints. The starting value is 25%; raise it for long, complex, or high-volume jobs.","As a business starting point, Tenkai recommends at least 70% profit on material and the failure reserve. Adjust it for risk, quality, market, and delivery responsibility.","In both apps, enter the whole percentage: 70 for 70%, 25 for 25%, and 120 for 120%.","Do not lower the price only because quantity increases: large projects also increase the cost of reprinting failures and delivering consistent quality."],t.s)
A.aTD=new B.am("application","MATERIAL AND PROFIT","Set material, failures, and profit","Separate production costs from what the business must earn.",A.aI0,"Profit applies only to material and the failure reserve. Extras are added at their configured price; energy, depreciation, maintenance, and taxes are also charged separately.",null)
A.aHu=s(["In Machines, enter each device's wattage, real purchase price, and general maintenance cost.","Set a reasonable useful life and maintenance interval. The app distributes those amounts across operating hours.","Include cleaning, nozzles, films, lubricants, wear parts, and technical service in the relevant maintenance cost.","Configure washing and curing equipment as well when working with resin."],t.s)
A.aSl=new B.am("application","EQUIPMENT","Recover depreciation and maintenance","Every operating hour should help replace and maintain equipment.",A.aHu,"Depreciation and maintenance recover costs; they are not profit. Leaving them at zero can make an unprofitable price look safe.",null)
A.af0=s(["Research the tax rate for your activity and enter the local rate. In both apps, 16 means 16%.","Enable or apply tax only when it belongs on that customer's document.","Add design, modeling, post-processing, painting, labor, packaging, shipping, and other services as extras. Their price is independent and does not receive the material profit percentage.","When used, configure isopropyl alcohol, laser rates, and the recommended deposit with real operating values.","Run a sample calculation and review the full breakdown before quoting: material, failures, energy, equipment, maintenance, extras, profit, and tax."],t.s)
A.aT_=new B.am("application","TAXES AND EXTRAS","Complete country-specific costs","Taxes, services, and consumables are not profit.",A.af0,"The app helps calculate prices, but it does not replace local accounting, tax, or electricity guidance.",null)
